WEBVTT

00:00:06.610 --> 00:00:08.760
Lost Technologies.

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:10.540
The Great Pyramids of Egypt.

00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:12.250
The Nazca Lines.

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:14.840
Machu Picchu, the city in the sky.

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:20.840
How and why these wonders were created remain a mystery to this day.

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:24.710
Time marches on, and they outlive their purposes.

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:32.020
These now meaningless monuments are doomed to obscurity.

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:16.740
It's raining cats and dogs.

00:02:17.140 --> 00:02:18.990
Of all the places to be stuck at...

00:02:19.490 --> 00:02:21.740
I wonder if it's really worth it to just stay put?

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:24.830
It was so nice this afternoon, too.

00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:26.750
‘Guess it's just abnormal weather.

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:28.530
Must be “Gang Rain”, huh?

00:02:28.530 --> 00:02:30.090
<i>Guerrilla Rain</i>, stupid.

00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:33.670
Well you're surrounded and can't get away, just like with gangs, right?

00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:35.420
What kind of reasoning is that?

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:45.810
The forecast said it wouldn't rain today.

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:48.750
The one I saw said it would.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:49.770
Huh? How's that possible?

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:52.520
Each weatherman's prediction is a little different.

00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:55.320
So who's the genius weatherman you saw?

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:56.860
Like I’d remember!

00:02:56.860 --> 00:03:00.180
Do weathermen have, like, batting averages or something?

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:03.480
“This guy's strong in the summer, but stinks at predicting snow” or something...

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:06.040
Then I'd watch the best one before I leave for school.

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:08.210
Sounds like the bookkeepers at horse races.

00:03:08.210 --> 00:03:09.500
By the way, Senpai.

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:10.250
Yeah?

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:14.400
If you knew it was gonna rain, where's your umbrella?

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:16.440
Forgot it at school.

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:23.280
It's coming down pretty hard considering it was unexpected.

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:25.470
Doesn't look like it'll clear up anytime soon.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:30.190
I'm getting kinda chilly...

00:03:30.190 --> 00:03:32.230
Yeah, our clothes are basically soaked.

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:34.860
Rain this time of year is pretty cold.

00:03:36.610 --> 00:03:39.630
Hey, since we're right in front of the laundromat,

00:03:39.630 --> 00:03:41.920
let's throw our clothes in the dryer real quick!

00:03:42.250 --> 00:03:44.700
We're gonna catch a cold at this rate.

00:03:45.090 --> 00:03:46.850
Hold it.

00:03:46.850 --> 00:03:49.250
What're you planning on wearing while your clothes are drying?

00:03:50.130 --> 00:03:52.380
Do you ever think before you speak?

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:54.070
We'll be fine.

00:03:54.070 --> 00:03:56.600
Nobody's gonna come when it's pouring rain like this.

00:03:56.600 --> 00:03:57.640
Come on, Tattsun, let's do it.

00:03:57.640 --> 00:03:59.250
Huh!? No way!

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:00.130
Not happening!

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:01.440
You'll be fine!

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:04.010
Hurry, before you catch cold.

00:04:05.510 --> 00:04:08.270
No! I'm not gonna do it!

00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:15.110
If someone comes, you have to cover us.

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:21.740
Wouldn't it be more effective if Tattsun's <i>nice body</i> was distracting them instead?

00:04:21.740 --> 00:04:24.230
No way. I'm way to good to just let anyone see me like that.

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:25.780
You do it.

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:29.460
In that case, Kon-senpai's got nothing to worry about hiding.

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:32.750
That was a nice, clean hit.

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:37.100
Well, excuse me for not having anything.

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:40.050
That's his only option left.

00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:43.070
I feel so icky wearing wet underwear.

00:04:43.070 --> 00:04:45.680
How about borrowing those? They look pretty dry.

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:48.440
Not a chance! Who knows who they belong to?

00:04:48.440 --> 00:04:51.050
We should have thrown our underwear in too.

00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:52.940
What were you planning to do if someone comes in?

00:04:58.570 --> 00:05:01.170
What are you doing, Senpai?

00:05:01.170 --> 00:05:03.790
Feels kinda liberating, doesn't it?

00:05:06.950 --> 00:05:08.870
They're still kinda damp though...

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:10.480
Still better than before.

00:05:10.480 --> 00:05:12.050
A little warm, too.

00:05:15.140 --> 00:05:16.430
I'm cold...

00:05:16.430 --> 00:05:18.550
That warmth sure didn't last long.

00:05:18.550 --> 00:05:21.460
Wet clothes really sap your body heat.

00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:23.210
Why didn't you tell me that earlier?

00:05:26.230 --> 00:05:29.540
Sure looks nice and warm inside there.

00:05:29.540 --> 00:05:32.590
I won't stop you, so go ahead and make yourself a fried pervert.

00:05:32.590 --> 00:05:33.960
That'd be great!

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:36.290
You love those weird murder cases, right?

00:05:36.290 --> 00:05:38.820
I'm not in any hurry to become a corpse.

00:05:39.960 --> 00:05:43.030
I've had it! I'll just drink something hot.

00:05:44.570 --> 00:05:46.530
They're all cold drinks!

00:05:46.530 --> 00:05:48.450
Guess they haven't stocked the warm stuff yet.

00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:51.550
Quit goofing off, you piece of crap!

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:53.780
Make with the HOT coffee already!

00:05:53.780 --> 00:05:56.420
A lazy employee like you shouldn’t talk.

00:05:56.420 --> 00:05:58.660
They’ve got an udon machine here.

00:05:58.660 --> 00:05:59.480
I'll take it!

00:05:59.480 --> 00:06:01.660
As long as it's hot, I don't care what it is!

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:04.860
What exactly comes out of an udon machine?

00:06:04.860 --> 00:06:06.720
Cup udon, of course.

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:09.350
But there's no hot water spout on this.

00:06:11.010 --> 00:06:12.480
No hot water pots around, either.

00:06:12.520 --> 00:06:15.130
Gimme back my 300 yen!

00:06:15.130 --> 00:06:16.600
You're one unlucky customer.

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:19.090
Nothing's coming out at all...

00:06:19.090 --> 00:06:20.770
My precious 300 yen...

00:06:20.770 --> 00:06:23.860
Hey, sounds like something's moving inside it.

00:06:23.860 --> 00:06:26.500
Maybe it got stuck or something.

00:06:27.350 --> 00:06:28.550
What is it?

00:06:28.550 --> 00:06:29.450
It's moving.

00:06:29.450 --> 00:06:31.280
It's making the udon inside there.

00:06:31.280 --> 00:06:32.120
What?

00:06:33.370 --> 00:06:34.400
There it is!

00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:35.530
What the heck?

00:06:35.530 --> 00:06:37.370
Looks like Fox Udon.

00:06:41.420 --> 00:06:43.500
This Fox Udon's piping hot.

00:06:43.550 --> 00:06:45.010
This isn't cup udon.

00:06:45.010 --> 00:06:46.800
And it's faster too!

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:50.420
You may think this looks old and crummy,

00:06:50.420 --> 00:06:53.100
but maybe it's really a futuristic machine from outer space.

00:06:54.600 --> 00:06:55.840
I'm gonna try it again.

00:06:55.840 --> 00:06:57.150
How many do you plan on having?

00:06:57.150 --> 00:06:58.970
I wanna watch the machine make it!

00:06:58.970 --> 00:07:00.370
What is this, an arcade game?

00:07:01.490 --> 00:07:03.450
It's cool, I'll have one myself.

00:07:03.450 --> 00:07:04.980
I need something hot anyway.

00:07:10.780 --> 00:07:12.080
Hey, there it is.

00:07:12.680 --> 00:07:14.520
It's pouring the hot water.

00:07:14.520 --> 00:07:16.910
It's even stopping at the right time.

00:07:17.210 --> 00:07:19.250
There it goes again.

00:07:19.250 --> 00:07:22.320
Wow, it steamed it twice!

00:07:22.320 --> 00:07:23.840
Here comes the broth.

00:07:24.390 --> 00:07:25.340
All done!

00:07:25.340 --> 00:07:27.630
Hmm, that's pretty cool.

00:07:28.140 --> 00:07:28.910
Ouch!

00:07:28.910 --> 00:07:31.020
The taste is mediocre, though.

00:07:31.020 --> 00:07:33.640
Hey, what about the hamburger machine?

00:07:35.350 --> 00:07:36.920
I'll try it out!

00:07:36.920 --> 00:07:38.770
Ooh, lemme see! Lemme see!

00:07:40.980 --> 00:07:44.100
Well, is it making it inside there?

00:07:44.100 --> 00:07:45.020
I can't see...

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:48.870
Rats. Pre-packaged, huh?

00:07:48.870 --> 00:07:50.910
“Ready” just means it's warmed up.

00:07:50.910 --> 00:07:51.980
Hot!

00:07:51.980 --> 00:07:53.990
The box nearly burned me!

00:07:53.990 --> 00:07:56.510
These future folk don't know how to tone it down.

00:07:56.510 --> 00:07:58.540
I thought they were aliens.

00:08:00.440 --> 00:08:02.680
This box looks kinda dodgy...

00:08:02.680 --> 00:08:04.410
What's inside is the important part.

00:08:06.170 --> 00:08:08.310
Looks more like a shamburger to me.

00:08:08.310 --> 00:08:10.230
Who are you calling a shamburger!?

00:08:10.230 --> 00:08:12.010
Why are you so mad?

00:08:12.010 --> 00:08:14.800
I bet it's made with the finest ingredients!

00:08:15.020 --> 00:08:16.030
Ingredients.

00:08:16.030 --> 00:08:23.690
Meat: beef, pork, chicken, mutton, horse, rabbit, etc.

00:08:23.690 --> 00:08:26.900
See? So many ingredients, it must be top-class!

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:29.590
What's that say about the places with 100% beef?

00:08:29.590 --> 00:08:32.230
More importantly, since they wrote rabbit on there,

00:08:32.230 --> 00:08:34.490
I'm kinda curious about what the “etc.” means.

00:08:34.490 --> 00:08:39.500
You know, how at night when the workers sneak a peek inside the fridge...

00:08:39.500 --> 00:08:42.040
I know, “Meowburger”, right?

00:08:42.040 --> 00:08:45.550
You're kinda cat-like, so wouldn't it be cannibalism?

00:08:45.550 --> 00:08:47.100
That's just an urban legend.

00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:49.840
Cats are actually more costly and troublesome to use.

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:51.930
There's the one about lizard parts too.

00:08:51.930 --> 00:08:54.070
They’re considered high-quality ingredients in some places.

00:08:54.070 --> 00:08:55.930
Which Iron Chef decided that?

00:08:57.220 --> 00:08:59.930
Okay, I'll try a ham and cheese toast.

00:09:03.770 --> 00:09:05.560
Ow! Ouch, ouch, ouch.

00:09:05.560 --> 00:09:07.430
Isn't all this stuff a bit too hot?

00:09:07.430 --> 00:09:09.780
Those aliens need to take it down a notch.

00:09:09.780 --> 00:09:13.800
Look, it says, “risk of burn, use caution" right there.

00:09:13.800 --> 00:09:16.050
What, no Esperanto?

00:09:16.050 --> 00:09:16.990
Esper-what?

00:09:16.990 --> 00:09:18.580
The official language of Earth.

00:09:22.030 --> 00:09:23.750
That was pretty yummy.

00:09:23.750 --> 00:09:25.610
Sure does warm you up.

00:09:25.610 --> 00:09:29.160
It tastes much better when you add a fun-factor to it, huh?

00:09:29.160 --> 00:09:32.930
I don't think the guys who made this had entertainment in mind.

00:09:33.090 --> 00:09:33.970
That's it!

00:09:33.970 --> 00:09:37.640
What Seaside needs is that very same fun-factor!

00:09:37.640 --> 00:09:42.390
If it’s got fun, then even that crappy, bland coffee would taste better!

00:09:42.390 --> 00:09:47.770
Fun-factor or no, isn't figuring out how to improve the coffee more important?

00:09:47.770 --> 00:09:49.150
Oh, I think it stopped.

00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:17.200
This fresh laundry smells the best!

00:10:21.850 --> 00:10:23.870
I'm hungry.

00:10:27.570 --> 00:10:32.520
Times like this are when this hidden little oasis really comes through.

00:10:38.290 --> 00:10:40.610
The lost arts of ancient civilizations.

00:10:41.510 --> 00:10:46.400
Monuments fated some day to be forgotten by man.

00:10:46.400 --> 00:10:50.620
But until that day, they continue to thrive among society.

00:10:54.510 --> 00:10:58.020
Just look at it simmer.

00:11:01.040 --> 00:11:02.040
I can't get it open!

00:11:02.040 --> 00:11:04.220
Hey Sanada-kun...

00:11:04.230 --> 00:11:06.260
Sorry, but could you open this for me?

00:11:06.260 --> 00:11:07.580
Yeah, sure.

00:11:07.580 --> 00:11:08.690
Thanks!

00:11:08.690 --> 00:11:10.860
Even though you're a customer...

00:11:10.860 --> 00:11:12.460
Thanks so much!

00:11:12.460 --> 00:11:15.230
‘Gotta leave the tough work to the boys, right?

00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:27.320
What's wrong?

00:11:27.590 --> 00:11:28.990
A jar! Find me a jar!

00:11:28.990 --> 00:11:30.550
A really hard to open one!

00:11:30.550 --> 00:11:32.000
I'll make Sanada-kun open it for me!

00:11:33.630 --> 00:11:34.470
Found one!

00:11:42.120 --> 00:11:44.010
JAR!

00:11:46.370 --> 00:11:48.020
Wow, you're like a widow!

00:11:48.020 --> 00:11:49.380
Don't talk like I'm some kind of butch!

00:11:49.990 --> 00:11:50.680
That's...

00:11:51.220 --> 00:11:53.040
Quit screwin' around!

00:11:53.040 --> 00:11:54.520
Yes ma'am.

00:11:57.040 --> 00:12:00.060
Head Maid, your stocking's torn.

00:12:00.550 --> 00:12:01.370
Huh?

00:12:01.370 --> 00:12:02.410
Oh dear.

00:12:08.350 --> 00:12:09.870
Hey, what the heck?

00:12:10.830 --> 00:12:13.130
Hustleryuki, don't tell me you're...

00:12:13.840 --> 00:12:14.790
No! That's not-

00:12:14.790 --> 00:12:18.050
No! Sanada-kun's hot for the head maid!?

00:12:20.380 --> 00:12:23.130
A nightmare engraved into my mind.

00:12:23.130 --> 00:12:25.500
I have laid eyes upon that which isn’t to be witnessed.

00:12:25.500 --> 00:12:27.560
Today, we mourn for Sanada.

00:12:27.560 --> 00:12:31.560
Osaka's famous for its street food.

00:12:33.810 --> 00:12:38.060
With the change in the everyday drudgery, all students, without exception...

00:12:38.730 --> 00:12:40.810
...gradually begin buzzing with excitement this time of year.

00:12:41.540 --> 00:12:44.190
The season of the culture festival.

00:12:47.150 --> 00:12:51.870
It's not even for a whole ‘nother month yet, but everyone's running around preparing for the festival.

00:12:51.870 --> 00:12:55.230
Some people plan their whole year around the culture festival.

00:12:55.230 --> 00:12:56.160
How childish.

00:12:56.820 --> 00:12:58.410
Childish, huh?

00:12:58.410 --> 00:13:00.240
Well, not really...

00:13:00.240 --> 00:13:03.080
How come our class isn't doing anything?

00:13:03.080 --> 00:13:04.580
I wanna be a part of the festivities!

00:13:05.330 --> 00:13:08.970
A lot of our classmates are busy contributing to their clubs’ booths.

00:13:08.970 --> 00:13:10.880
There's just not enough free hands.

00:13:10.880 --> 00:13:13.670
Let's all do something next year. The whole class!

00:13:13.670 --> 00:13:17.810
We only have so many chances to be a part of the culture festival.

00:13:17.810 --> 00:13:20.180
You do have a point.

00:13:20.930 --> 00:13:22.650
How about we put on a play?

00:13:23.260 --> 00:13:24.520
I'll write the script.

00:13:24.520 --> 00:13:26.730
I've got tons of great ideas.

00:13:26.730 --> 00:13:29.040
Like “Murder on Jell-O Island”.

00:13:30.360 --> 00:13:32.690
I bet you're gonna have me killed off, right?

00:13:32.690 --> 00:13:33.860
Uncle! Uncle!

00:13:40.750 --> 00:13:42.820
Hell yeah! Stage ticket!

00:13:46.660 --> 00:13:48.670
Gimme some curry and coffee.

00:13:48.670 --> 00:13:49.550
Yes'm.

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:52.400
It's “yes ma'am”, not “yes'm”.

00:13:52.400 --> 00:13:54.260
Don't get sloppy just ‘cause she's our friend.

00:13:54.260 --> 00:13:55.050
Yes'm.

00:13:56.380 --> 00:13:59.140
So? You got what now?

00:13:59.140 --> 00:14:01.490
You got a stagecoach or something?

00:14:01.490 --> 00:14:03.830
<i>Stage</i>, not stagecoach, retard.

00:14:04.260 --> 00:14:07.290
Kon-senpai made a pretty nice comeback, don't you think?

00:14:07.290 --> 00:14:08.940
I didn't get it at all.

00:14:09.310 --> 00:14:13.120
I won a stage spot on day three from the raffle.

00:14:13.120 --> 00:14:14.280
Let's put together a band.

00:14:15.900 --> 00:14:18.500
I'm kinda nervous singing in front of a crowd.

00:14:18.500 --> 00:14:20.240
Who said you clowns would be singing?

00:14:20.240 --> 00:14:21.950
Yeah, you're tone deaf anyway.

00:14:23.240 --> 00:14:26.370
You've never even listened to me sing!

00:14:26.370 --> 00:14:28.990
Don't need to. You can tell by your face.

00:14:28.990 --> 00:14:31.520
Well, you're actually a little better than tone-deaf.

00:14:32.210 --> 00:14:33.500
How do you know that!?

00:14:33.500 --> 00:14:38.030
Have you been to karaoke with her before?

00:14:38.030 --> 00:14:40.580
I've got vocals and bass under control.

00:14:40.580 --> 00:14:42.110
You guys pick an instrument.

00:14:42.110 --> 00:14:44.770
You can play guitar or keyboard, can't you?

00:14:44.770 --> 00:14:46.540
Don't just assume everyone can play.

00:14:46.540 --> 00:14:47.680
Yeah!

00:14:47.680 --> 00:14:48.510
Hotori.

00:14:49.100 --> 00:14:52.520
What about that one I taught you in grade school? You know...

00:14:52.520 --> 00:14:57.650
Oh yeah! I can play something keyboard-like.

00:14:57.650 --> 00:15:03.280
Come to think of it, I used to play something guitar-ish a while back.

00:15:03.280 --> 00:15:04.260
For real?

00:15:05.280 --> 00:15:08.790
I can't believe I found members this easily!

00:15:08.790 --> 00:15:10.790
I got the drummer taken care of too.

00:15:14.010 --> 00:15:16.050
You're a genius, Kon-senpai!

00:15:17.800 --> 00:15:21.310
Haribara, you've got excessive lower-body movement,

00:15:21.310 --> 00:15:23.680
so you tend to run outta steam in the second half.

00:15:23.680 --> 00:15:26.980
So I've come up with a special training exercise to build up your lower body

00:15:26.980 --> 00:15:30.850
and your upper body strength at the same time.

00:15:30.850 --> 00:15:31.850
Senpai!

00:15:35.970 --> 00:15:38.490
Sweet! We got us a band!

00:15:38.970 --> 00:15:42.490
There's a catch, so this'll be fun.

00:15:45.490 --> 00:15:47.820
I knew it was too good to be true.

00:15:47.820 --> 00:15:50.450
Getting all excited without even seeing you in action.

00:15:51.090 --> 00:15:56.500
Even by a loose...A VERY loose interpretation, an accordion's hardly like a keyboard.

00:15:56.500 --> 00:15:57.670
Well, whatever.

00:15:58.380 --> 00:16:01.190
You call that a guitar!?

00:16:01.190 --> 00:16:02.800
See? It's got strings too.

00:16:02.800 --> 00:16:04.910
If anything with strings is a guitar,

00:16:04.910 --> 00:16:08.590
then a harp, koto, or even a triangle is a damn guitar!

00:16:08.590 --> 00:16:11.940
They don't use strings, they're triangle-shaped.

00:16:11.940 --> 00:16:13.560
Yeah, triangle.

00:16:13.560 --> 00:16:16.070
You're just repeating me to sound smart, aren't you?

00:16:17.070 --> 00:16:19.080
Ah, screw it.

00:16:19.080 --> 00:16:21.860
I'm just thankful you're willing to perform with me.

00:16:21.860 --> 00:16:24.290
Can't say we're not creative, I guess.

00:16:29.580 --> 00:16:32.860
It's so tiring keeping up with Kon-senpai's selfishness.

00:16:32.860 --> 00:16:35.580
You sure look like you're having fun, though.

00:16:35.580 --> 00:16:41.070
Just the fact that this'll keep up until the festival is giving me a migraine.

00:16:41.840 --> 00:16:45.090
Then again, it's good that they're giving it their all.

00:16:46.100 --> 00:16:49.770
Hey, you running a dying cat-fé now?

00:16:49.770 --> 00:16:51.520
It's a karaoke café.

00:16:51.520 --> 00:16:52.980
Go on, belt one out.

00:17:05.240 --> 00:17:07.530
Which one of you guys drew this?

00:17:07.530 --> 00:17:08.780
He did.

00:17:08.980 --> 00:17:10.890
You're pretty good!

00:17:10.890 --> 00:17:11.950
T-Thanks...

00:17:12.370 --> 00:17:13.790
What about this 4-panel one?

00:17:13.790 --> 00:17:15.540
Oh, that was me.

00:17:15.540 --> 00:17:17.070
This is really neat.

00:17:17.070 --> 00:17:17.960
Thank you!

00:17:18.670 --> 00:17:23.120
Oops, forgot I was going to buy some octopus balls and Korean pancakes.

00:17:23.120 --> 00:17:25.800
Octopus, pancakes; 1, 2, 3!

00:17:26.330 --> 00:17:27.530
You're not gonna buy it!?

00:17:29.400 --> 00:17:34.300
Let's see...spring rolls are on the 3rd floor, gymnastics clubroom.

00:17:35.450 --> 00:17:38.220
Tatsuno, the grilled chicken stand is out by the field.

00:17:38.220 --> 00:17:40.140
Let's hurry up and buy some so we can eat.

00:17:40.810 --> 00:17:42.720
Now, what was I supposed to get...

00:17:42.720 --> 00:17:43.530
Umm...

00:17:43.530 --> 00:17:47.750
Actually, I wanted to see the festival with you...

00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:48.530
What?

00:17:52.020 --> 00:17:55.160
I am NOT fat. I'm just growing.

00:17:55.500 --> 00:17:58.950
I mean, I realize it myself,

00:17:58.950 --> 00:18:03.260
that sometimes I'm being over-confident and egotistical.

00:18:03.260 --> 00:18:06.730
And ‘cause of that, I get depressed.

00:18:06.730 --> 00:18:09.180
So you see... umm...

00:18:09.180 --> 00:18:13.140
I'll still try my very best to play tomorrow...

00:18:13.140 --> 00:18:15.180
Umm...

00:18:15.180 --> 00:18:18.520
You don't even have to ask. I'll come see you.

00:18:21.520 --> 00:18:24.690
Ohmigod! I practically confessed to him!

00:18:25.120 --> 00:18:28.680
Tatsuno's trying her hardest to beat her depression, huh?

00:18:29.440 --> 00:18:31.700
I've gotta cheer her on.

00:18:33.220 --> 00:18:35.880
What the heck are those two doing?

00:18:35.910 --> 00:18:38.940
Can't even count on them to go on a food run.

00:18:38.940 --> 00:18:42.440
The octopus balls and pancakes are gonna get cold!

00:18:47.220 --> 00:18:50.160
Full-volume lullaby!

00:18:50.160 --> 00:18:52.020
Okay, last day!

00:18:52.020 --> 00:18:55.020
Price down from 200 to 50 yen!

00:18:55.020 --> 00:18:56.870
Sorry, sold out!

00:18:56.870 --> 00:18:59.520
Gymnastics club is officially closed!

00:19:04.820 --> 00:19:07.470
You don't even have to ask. I'll come see you.

00:19:09.120 --> 00:19:11.510
Why did I have to ask him that?

00:19:11.510 --> 00:19:13.370
You nervous or somethin', Tatsuno-san?

00:19:13.370 --> 00:19:16.950
Don't sweat it. Just like we practiced.

00:19:16.950 --> 00:19:18.470
The rest will come naturally!

00:19:19.250 --> 00:19:21.830
I-I'm not nervous or anything!

00:19:21.830 --> 00:19:23.630
Just keep your mouth shut, blowfish cheeks!

00:19:23.630 --> 00:19:24.380
B-BLOWFISH CHEEKS!?

00:19:24.380 --> 00:19:26.920
I've never been so insulted in all my life!

00:19:26.920 --> 00:19:32.010
I'm not letting that one slide, you haughty four-eyed—

00:19:32.010 --> 00:19:33.260
Knock it off, guys!

00:19:33.260 --> 00:19:35.560
Even I got tricked into playing the drums!

00:19:35.560 --> 00:19:36.640
Stupid fake training!

00:19:36.640 --> 00:19:37.980
That's got nothing to do with this!

00:19:40.230 --> 00:19:42.500
Dammit guys, quit bickering!

00:19:43.680 --> 00:19:45.950
Don't pull this crap right before the show.

00:19:45.950 --> 00:19:47.200
Kon-senpai!

00:19:47.990 --> 00:19:50.600
W-We lose!

00:19:50.600 --> 00:19:52.240
Whoa... déjà vu.

00:19:52.240 --> 00:19:54.740
Okay, please get ready.

00:19:54.760 --> 00:19:58.720
I practice my shuriken skills before bed.

00:20:00.660 --> 00:20:03.880
All right, taking the stage next...!

00:20:03.880 --> 00:20:08.360
...is a 4-girl band, “The Maids”!

00:20:08.360 --> 00:20:12.640
After hours of debate, they chose to don their maid outfits,

00:20:12.640 --> 00:20:14.040
thus, they have become “The Maids”.

00:20:14.040 --> 00:20:16.600
Okay girls, take it away!

00:20:24.470 --> 00:20:28.160
Don't believe what I say,

00:20:28.160 --> 00:20:32.200
I'm leaving for good.

00:20:32.200 --> 00:20:35.680
As clouds float across the southern skies,

00:20:35.680 --> 00:20:40.060
farewell to those halcyon days.

00:20:40.740 --> 00:20:42.040
Who's that singing?

00:20:42.370 --> 00:20:43.180
That's Kon!

00:20:43.180 --> 00:20:43.920
No way!

00:20:43.960 --> 00:20:45.960
Go Maids!

00:20:47.880 --> 00:20:49.240
It wasn't supposed to be like this!

00:20:49.750 --> 00:20:51.210
I didn't mean to do it!

00:20:51.690 --> 00:20:53.200
You call this rock!?

00:20:53.680 --> 00:20:54.890
This ain't rock!

00:20:55.900 --> 00:20:59.410
They're right, but it still has the same energy to it.

00:20:59.410 --> 00:21:03.380
What's that say on her apron? Seaside?

00:21:03.380 --> 00:21:05.470
Kon-senpai!

00:21:05.470 --> 00:21:07.440
It's pretty catchy, don'tcha think?

00:21:07.440 --> 00:21:09.220
This song's a little too hipster for me.

00:21:09.220 --> 00:21:11.240
Careful, you'll piss off the hipsters!

00:21:11.240 --> 00:21:14.990
But we don't care, we'll keep playing.

00:21:14.990 --> 00:21:19.080
There's someone waiting for me at the edge of the world.

00:21:19.080 --> 00:21:22.820
The winds may not carry our sound too far,

00:21:22.820 --> 00:21:26.830
but it'll last through the Ides of March.

00:21:26.830 --> 00:21:30.740
We're the world-famous sassy maids!

00:21:30.740 --> 00:21:34.630
Sowing chaos and disorder through the universe.

00:21:34.630 --> 00:21:38.480
We'll bop you one right here and now!

00:21:38.480 --> 00:21:42.430
See ya later, alligator! Get lost Pluto!

00:21:45.600 --> 00:21:48.800
“Oi”, not “hoi”, dammit!

00:21:54.360 --> 00:21:55.190
And so...

00:21:56.440 --> 00:22:00.200
After the cleanup, when we return to school,

00:22:02.020 --> 00:22:05.930
there remains not even a trace of the vibrant festival that just took place.

00:23:41.970 --> 00:23:43.110
Hey, get this!

00:23:43.110 --> 00:23:48.390
After I ate this bean bun from the candy store, I won a freebie for the first time ever!

00:23:48.390 --> 00:23:50.980
Where's it say you've won on a bean bun?

00:23:50.980 --> 00:23:52.390
When you bite into it, instead of bean paste,

00:23:52.390 --> 00:23:54.190
you get a ball that says “winner”!

00:23:54.190 --> 00:23:56.220
Then you can turn it in an get another one!

00:23:56.220 --> 00:24:00.010
So all you get is the bread?

00:24:00.010 --> 00:24:04.280
You're right! You get hosed by the prize and forget about the important part!

00:24:04.280 --> 00:24:06.250
Next time: 9th street.

00:24:06.250 --> 00:24:08.190
Clash of the Buyitans!

00:24:08.190 --> 00:24:10.870
Round and round, nice 'n soft.
